  "body": "Phase 3 (closing audit) of design #3282 — \"a mirror is what it can prove\" (design doc: `files/designs/code-github-backup-mirror-contract.md` in the keep-the-four-repos-healthy goal workspace). Filed by the design architect, pass 29 (2026-10-31). **Gated on Phases 1–2 of the design** (Phase 1 = #3238 + #3233; Phase 2 = #3250 + #3219 + #3270 + #3257) and on its own phase siblings #3240 + #3229 landing the `ghb_common` state helpers and plan retention it audits against.\n\n## Scope\n\n1. **Closing inventory.** Grep `infra/github-backup/bin/` for every remaining bare `json.load` on a generated-state file and every `open(..., \"w\")` / `json.dump` write to one (`plan.json`, `state.json`, `MANIFEST.json`, `clone-status.jsonl` appends excluded — append-only logs are not in the torn-write class). Disposition each hit: migrated to the `ghb_common` helpers from #3240, or deliberately local with the reason recorded in this issue. The inventory is complete only when a fresh grep returns no undispositioned hits.\n2. **Named dispositions required:** (a) FAMILIES.md and the `reconcile-YYYY-MM-DD.md` report — markdown written non-atomically; expected disposition is migrate via the same atomic-write helper (a torn FAMILIES.md feeds cold-export decisions), or a recorded reason if not; (b) `drain_queue.py`'s per-repo `plan.json` re-read inside its fetch loop (a bare load and an O(events) re-read — disposition: route through the tolerant loader; restructuring the loop is in scope only if triage judges it trivial); (c) the Worker (`worker/src/index.js`) — expected disposition: out of scope with reason (KV is the store; the laptop half's ack discipline is Phase 2's #3219), recorded so the boundary is explicit.\n3. **Contract statement.** Write the design's seven rules, in operator language, into `infra/github-backup/README.md` (system contract section) and cross-reference from `docs/RUNBOOK.md` where the DR procedures consume MANIFEST.json — the docs are the system's system-of-record per #3215.\n4. **Evidence on the umbrella.** Post the completion evidence (inventory result, contract location, phase closure list) as a comment on #3215.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The grep inventory exists in this issue's closing comment with a disposition for every hit; a re-run grep finds no undispositioned bare load/write on generated state in `infra/github-backup/bin/`.\n- [ ] FAMILIES.md / reconcile-report, the drainer plan re-read, and the Worker boundary each carry an explicit disposition (migrated, or out-of-scope/local with reason).\n- [ ] README.md states the seven-rule contract and RUNBOOK.md cross-references it from the DR section.\n- [ ] Evidence comment posted on #3215 naming this design and its phase closures.\n- [ ] This audit does not re-open the decisions recorded on the design issue (validity = resolvability; four destination states; recorded outcomes; ack-on-ok; 3-consecutive-day streak; atomic state via `ghb_common`; plan retention) — a genuine blocker is flagged on the design issue instead.\n",
